{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1794","published":"2026-04-03T11:10:49Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:44.022294506Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-3195","CVE-2026-3196"],"summary":"qemu security update","details":"QEMU is a FAST! processor emulator using dynamic translation to achieve good emulation speed.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in QEMU. When reading input audio in the virtio-snd device input callback, the `virtio_snd_pcm_in_cb` function did not check whether the iov could fit the data buffer, potentially leading to a heap out-of-bounds write. This issue exists due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2024-7730.(CVE-2026-3195)\n\nAn integer overflow vulnerability was found in the virtio-snd device via PCM_INFO requests from the guest. A malicious guest can provide out-of-bounds stream counts, potentially leading to unbounded memory allocation on the host and a denial of service condition.(CVE-2026-3196)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"qemu","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP3","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/qemu&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP3"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["qemu-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-curl-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-iscsi-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-rbd-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-block-ssh-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-debuginfo-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-debugsource-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-guest-agent-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-hw-usb-host-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-img-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-aarch64-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-arm-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-riscv-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-system-x86_64-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-binfmt-8.2.0-72.oe2403sp3.aarch64.rpm","qemu-user-static-8.2.0-72.oe